1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:21,851
Twenty-five years ago from today, Ababa and Emama's very first grandson, Abush, lived with them. Back then in our house, when Ababa returned from work
he never sat at the table without seeing Abush; on one day, however, this story happened—lunch was ready and the yard stood silent.

2
00:00:21,892 --> 00:00:35,623
On that day, Abush had followed his friends down to the neighboring village since morning. Caught up in the heat of
the game, he completely forgot that the sun had reached mid-sky and Ababa's lunchtime had arrived.

3
00:00:35,617 --> 00:00:50,548
Right at noon, Ababa returned tired from work. The moment he leaned his walking stick against the wall,
his eyes scanned the yard—and raising his voice he asked, 'Emama! Where did Abush go?'

4
00:00:50,550 --> 00:01:02,641
Knowing Ababa's exhaustion and temper, Emama didn't flinch: 'Oh, he's playing right behind
the backyard; by the time you wash your hands and sit down, I'll call him.'

5
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:16,461
The second Ababa stepped inside and sat down, Emama tied her shawl tight around her waist and slipped out.
Under the blazing midday sun, she hurried like a young woman toward the neighboring village.

6
00:01:16,458 --> 00:01:27,709
When Emama found Abush sitting in the dust, she wasted no time—she hoisted him onto her back and
whispered, 'Hush, I told Ababa you're right here; let's get back before he notices!'

7
00:01:27,725 --> 00:01:45,016
Abush also lovingly called his grandmother Emama 'Ene.' Amazed by Emama's speed and the rush of the wind, Abush
clung to her back unable to hold back his laughter and cried out, 'Ene... you really are a leopard!'

8
00:01:45,033 --> 00:02:01,204
Just as Ababa uncovered the mesob to call them, both walked in catching their breath as if nothing had happened.
Ababa smiled seeing his first grandson—while Emama wiped her brow and quietly breathed a sigh of relief.

9
00:02:01,217 --> 00:02:17,788
Even 25 years from today, whenever Emama brings up that one-day memory, Ababa himself laughs—and for us, the name
'Ene, you are a leopard' that Abush gave Emama remained the lasting symbol of her love and speed.

10
00:02:17,775 --> 00:02:19,506
Ene, you are a leopard!
